***************************** T A L Y S **************************2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2522 1451
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2522 1451
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2522 1451
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2522 1451
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2522 1451
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2522 1451
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2522 1451
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2522 1451
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2522 1451
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2522 1451
stored in this data file:                                         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2522 1451
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2522 1451
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2522 1451
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2522 1451
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2522 1451
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2522 1451
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2522 1451
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2522 1451
- Recoil data                                                     2522 1451
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2522 1451
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2522 1451
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2522 1451
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2522 1451
- Residual production cross sections                              2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2522 1451
parameterization we refer to [kon12]. If for this specific        2522 1451
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2522 1451
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     2522 1451
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   2522 1451
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       2522 1451
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  2522 1451
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   2522 1451
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  2522 1451
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  2522 1451
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 2522 1451
to the highest incident energy.                                   2522 1451
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    2522 1451
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    2522 1451
total cross section.                                              2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   2522 1451
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        2522 1451
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     2522 1451
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         2522 1451
sections.                                                         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 2522 1451
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 2522 1451
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 2522 1451
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 2522 1451
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      2522 1451
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       2522 1451
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              2522 1451
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  2522 1451
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  2522 1451
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  2522 1451
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  2522 1451
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  2522 1451
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       2522 1451
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        2522 1451
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2522 1451
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        2522 1451
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2522 1451
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        2522 1451
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        2522 1451
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        2522 1451
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       2522 1451
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    2522 1451
discrete levels.                                                  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  2522 1451
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   2522 1451
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      2522 1451
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  2522 1451
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      2522 1451
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         2522 1451
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   2522 1451
on an angular grid.                                               2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       2522 1451
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        2522 1451
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2522 1451
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2522 1451
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         2522 1451
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     2522 1451
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   2522 1451
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  2522 1451
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             2522 1451
All data are generated with TALYS.                                2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      2522 1451
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   2522 1451
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   2522 1451
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are2522 1451
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   2522 1451
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  2522 1451
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              2522 1451
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 2522 1451
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  2522 1451
For each residual product:                                        2522 1451
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               2522 1451
- the recoil                                                      2522 1451
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         2522 1451
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     2522 1451
sections.                                                         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  2522 1451
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 2522 1451
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          2522 1451
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       2522 1451
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 2522 1451
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     2522 1451
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  2522 1451
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      2522 1451
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         2522 1451
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   2522 1451
followed:                                                         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2522 1451
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2522 1451
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         2522 1451
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     2522 1451
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2522 1451
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2522 1451
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2522 1451
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2522 1451
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    2522 1451
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          2522 1451
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     2522 1451
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     2522 1451
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    2522 1451
as isomer.                                                        2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        2522 1451
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    2522 1451
as isomer.                                                        2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:2522 1451
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   2522 1451
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   2522 1451
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   2522 1451
  given                                                           2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        2522 1451
and more details are given above in this description.             2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  2522 1451
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     2522 1451
with the TASMAN code [kon12], which generates TALYS runs using    2522 1451
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   2522 1451
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  2522 1451
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                2522 1451
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      2522 1451
   same reaction channel between different energies)              2522 1451
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      2522 1451
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               2522 1451
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      2522 1451
   different reaction channels for different energies)            2522 1451
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        2522 1451
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              2522 1451
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  2522 1451
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       2522 1451
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     2522 1451
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  2522 1451
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     2522 1451
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     2522 1451
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     2522 1451
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   2522 1451
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   2522 1451
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  2522 1451
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       2522 1451
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  2522 1451
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon12], which generates       2522 1451
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   2522 1451
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         2522 1451
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  2522 1451
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      2522 1451
representation is used.                                           2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  2522 1451
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             2522 1451
                                                                  2522 1451
